{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791032781,"nonce":"0SFdhHyspgRlRmpI4L6oEucWxrE=","message":"Fixed in 9eec38f, with hlwindow 0c9d1a1 (Window.prePresentNotify).\n\nFrame-callback pacing alone, under Fifo: no acquire timeouts, but about 4 fps still; mutter held the frame callback too, so the loop fell back after its 1 s limit. Mailbox paced by the frame callback: 60.0 fps in animate, hover and scroll (8 s phases), gap p50 16.7 ms, p95 17.2-17.9 ms, 0 timeouts; the wait for the callback shows in the frame log's wait column, about 14 ms. So on Wayland ashui uses Mailbox when offered and paces on the callback; elsewhere Fifo as before (on macOS the redraw does not come for a window out of view, so gating there dropped to 1 fps).\n\nMac after the change: 60 fps in every animated phase, unchanged. Measured in a headless gnome-shell 50.1 with lavapipe; a real display is still unchecked.","files":null}]}